+# BR-BAR-003 — A record counts once
+
+| Field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Status | illustrative |
+| Layer | silver |
+| Implementation | `int_bar__records` (dbt) |
+| GSBPM | 5.4 Edit and impute |
+
+## Definition
+
+A record is identified by `record_id`. When the Foo System sends a record again, the record keeps its
+**first reception** and the later ones do not count. Written after the edition of February 2026 was blocked
+by control CK-01: the source had sent the whole of January a second time.
